          "stageRecord": "First, those two students moves from the embedded Spec-IP already present to matrix Spec-IP, leaving a silent intermediate DP trace. Finite I assigns nominative Case and licenses third-person plural agreement on seem. The completed A-chain connects this Case position through the embedded subject trace to the Theme position under invited; it contains no additional theta role or control dependency. Only then adjoins as AdvP to the completed matrix IP, producing an outer IP segment. Unlike the DP-attached analysis, Only is not a member of the raised constituent: it has the matrix proposition as its structural scope domain and associates with the subject focus. Its alternatives are propositions differing in the relevant subject, so this reading can overlap truth-conditionally with nominal Only while remaining structurally distinct. It does not require an unpronounced occurrence of Only inside the infinitive. The final pronounced sequence exactly matches all nine input tokens.",
          "statement": "Complete subject raising and adjoin Only to the finite IP with subject-focused association.",
